+# K16 ray theorem (T): `t=3`, `t=4`, and the uniform-coefficient attack
+
+**Lane:** `k16-t3-uniform-sol56-20260903`  
+**Date:** 2026-09-03  
+**Verdict:** fixed-`t` computations pending; the proposed fixed-band uniform
+obstruction is disproved by an exact subsystem point, and no uniform unit
+certificate is presently in hand.  
+**Scope:** theorem (T) on the K=16 ray at fixed `t=3` and `t=4`, followed by a
+generic-`t` coefficient-family audit. No ledger edit; no `jc2-lean`; no prohibited
+in-progress report read. Drivers and measurements are confined to
+`box/k16t3-20260903/`.
+
+Claim labels are literal. **MEASURED** records reproducible program output;
+**MEASURED-MODULAR** is evidence over named finite fields and is not a
+characteristic-zero proof; **DERIVED** is a displayed mathematical consequence;
+**PROVED-HERE** is an exact certificate or checked proof. `OPEN[...]` is not filled
+by analogy or by finitely many fixed-`t` computations.
+
+## 0. Custody and fail-closed gate
+
+**MEASURED.** The readable lane receipt
+`xmodel/k16-t3-uniform-sol56-20260903.run.v2` was parsed with `awk`. Its
+`charged_input_<i>_sha256` and `charged_input_<i>_basename` fields were paired,
+without retyping a hash, under `/tmp/jc2-lane.NKyBDU/inputs/`; the resulting
+manifest was passed to `sha256sum -c`. All **10/10** files returned `OK`. The
+content-mismatch stop did not fire.
+
+**MEASURED (scope).** Only the ten frozen inputs and new artifacts named in this
+report were read. Neither prohibited in-progress lane report was opened. There was
+no ledger edit, no `jc2-lean` access, and no `ideation-*` file access. All driver
+writes are under `box/k16t3-20260903/`; this report is the only `xmodel` write.
+
+## 1. The family and the generalized order chart
+
+### 1.1 Radii and denominator
+
+**DERIVED + MEASURED.** Put
+
+```text
+n=12t+4, m=8t+4, M2=12t+1, V2=3,
+e=n/4=3t+1, q=m/4=2t+1.
+```
+
+The frozen symbolic derivation simplifies Moh's Definition-5.1 values to
+
+```text
+delta2^51=-1/2, delta1^51=t/[2(3t+1)],
+(delta2',delta1')=(-1,t/(3t+1)).
+```
+
+It asserts these identities before specialization. Thus `t=3` gives
+`(-1,3/10)`, as requested, and `t=4` gives `(-1,4/13)`. Theorem 1.2 gives both
+coefficient families the common order bound
+
+```text
+ord C_i >= -i/e = -i/(3t+1).
+```
+
+### 1.2 Spaces, generator, and gauges
+
+**DERIVED.** With
+
+```text
+z=pi-gamma,
+B=pi*z+b1*pi+b2,
+A=pi*B+b3,
+h=pi*A+b4,
+```
+
+the intersection of the major- and minor-disc bounds gives
+
+| deficit `i` | coefficient space `S_i(t)` |
+|---:|---|
+| `1 <= i <= t` | `<1>` |
+| `t < i <= 2t` | `<1,A>` |
+| `2t < i <= 3t` | `<1,A,B>` |
+| `i=3t+1` | `<1,gamma,A,B,z>` |
+
+The generated chart is
+
+```text
+P=h^e + sum_(i=1)^e alpha_i h^(e-i),  alpha_i in S_i(t),
+Q=h^q + sum_(j=2)^q beta_j  h^(q-j),  beta_j  in S_j(t).
+```
+
+Here `beta_1=0` is the same approximate-root/Tschirnhausen normalization as in
+the charged generator. The nonzero second top-line coefficient is normalized to
+`-1`, as in that generator; `c!=0` is saturated explicitly.
+
+**PROVED-HERE (three safe target gauges).** Apply, in order,
+
+```text
+Q <- Q-const(beta_q),
+P <- P-alpha_t Q,
+P <- P-const(alpha_e).
+```
+
+The middle index is `e-q=t`: `alpha_t h^(e-t)=alpha_t h^q` aligns with the
+leading term of `Q`. Thus the charged `alpha_2=0` gauge generalizes to
+`alpha_t=0`, not to a fixed `alpha_2=0`. The scalar `alpha_t` induces changes
+`alpha_(t+j) <- alpha_(t+j)-alpha_t beta_j`; monotonicity
+`S_j(t) subset S_(t+j)(t)` keeps every changed coefficient in its declared
+space. The two endpoint operations are scalar target translations. The composite
+target map is invertible triangular with determinant one, so it preserves the
+Jacobian, degrees, monicity, and both-disc filtration. No parameter-dependent
+quantity is inverted.
+
+**DERIVED (counts).** Before gauging there are
+
+```text
+alpha: 6t+5, beta: 3t+2, b1..b4 and c: 5,
+total chart unknowns including c: 9t+12.
+```
+
+The gauges delete three scalar coordinates, giving `9t+9` unknowns: `36` at
+`t=3` and `45` at `t=4` (ungauged: `39` and `48`).
+
+**MEASURED (same generator).** The generalized driver specialized at `t=2`
+has exactly the same ordered parameter list, `P`, `Q`, 37 tagged coefficient
+equations, equation order, and Sympy expressions as the frozen
+`t2_order_system.py`. Deterministic numerical-parameter reconstruction of the
+full h-adic Jacobian is `True` at `t=2,3,4`.
+
+### 1.3 Exact banded identity
+
+**PROVED-HERE.** Set `alpha_0=beta_0=1`, `beta_1=0`. Before monic
+`h`-division, the raw coefficient at h-level `k` is
+
+```text
+R_k = sum_(e+q-i-j=k) J(beta_j,alpha_i)
+    + sum_(e+q-i-j-1=k)
+        [(e-i) alpha_i J(beta_j,h)
+         +(q-j) beta_j J(h,alpha_i)].
+```
+
+Starting with `C_0=0`, the driver performs the recurrence
+
+```text
+F_k=R_k+C_k = h*C_(k+1)+N_k,  deg_pi N_k<4,
+coeff(N_0-c*gamma)=0, coeff(N_k)=0 for k>0.
+```
+
+Division is Euclidean division in `pi` by the monic quartic `h`. Hence it is
+exact, divides by no parameter leader, and retains every zero-leader branch.
+
+## 2. Fixed `t=3`: `(40,28;37;3;J=c gamma)`
+
+Pending exact-Q computation.
+
+## 3. Fixed `t=4`: `(52,36;49;3;J=c gamma)`
+
+Pending modular and bounded exact-Q computations.
+
+## 4. Generic `t`: banded equations and coefficient dependence
+
+### 4.1 What is and is not `t`-dependent
+
+**DERIVED.** In deficit indexing, the only numerical coefficients involving `t`
+are `e-i=3t+1-i` and `q-j=2t+1-j`. Every generated numerical coefficient is
+therefore in `Z[t]`, of degree at most one. The Jacobians of the coefficient
+spaces, `z,B,A,h`, the monic carry, the target `c*gamma`, and the saturation
+equation are `t`-independent. The changing index ranges and the four regimes of
+`S_i(t)` are a separate combinatorial dependence. In particular, after the
+piecewise spaces have been declared, the order-chart ideal contains no
+`1/(3t+1)` or other rational function of `t`; no denominator saturation is
+needed merely to state this family.
+
+**DERIVED (reverse indexing).** Rename tail coefficients by h-power,
+
+```text
+p_s=alpha_(e-s), r_u=beta_(q-u).
+```
+
+Then a raw tail band has the literally `t`-independent form
+
+```text
+R_k^tail = sum_(u+s=k) J(r_u,p_s)
+         + sum_(u+s=k+1)
+             [s p_s J(r_u,h)+u r_u J(h,p_s)].
+```
+
+A final level `H` uses tail coefficients only through power `H+1`; their spaces
+have stabilized when `t>=H+1`. After the displayed canonical renaming, all
+generators through that level are then identical, not merely rational
+specializations.
+
+**MEASURED.** At `t=2,3,4` the equation counts are respectively `37,51,65`,
+matching `14t+9`; their exact level histograms match
+
+```text
+h=0:                     7
+h=1,...,t:               6 each
+h=t+1,...,2t:            5 each
+h=2t+1,...,3t+1:         2 each
+h=3t+2,...,4t+1:         1 each.
+```
+
+The scripts, rather than extrapolation from three values, remain the authority at
+each fixed `t`.
+
+### 4.2 High-side recurrence
+
+**DERIVED + MEASURED.** Let `a_1,b_1` be the `A` coordinates of
+`alpha_(t+1),beta_(t+1)`. The sole highest equation, at `h^(4t+1)`, is
+
+```text
+(2t+1)*a_1-(3t+1)*b_1=0.
+```
+
+The next equation, with the next `A` coordinates `a_2,b_2` and scalar
+`u_1=alpha_1`, is
+
+```text
+(2t+1)*a_2-(3t+1)*b_2-3t*u_1*b_1
+-b4*((2t+1)*a_1-(3t+1)*b_1)=0.
+```
+
+At `t=2,3,4` the leading equations are `5a_1-7b_1`, `7a_1-10b_1`, and
+`9a_1-13b_1`. Over `Q(t)`, `2t+1` and `3t+1` are safe pivots for positive
+integral `t`; this organizes the high coefficients recursively. It does not
+produce a unit, because the number of middle bands between this recurrence and
+the Jacobian tail grows with `t`.
+
+## 5. Low-band test and first nonuniform band
+
+### 5.1 Exact symbolic consistency witness
+
+**PROVED-HERE.** The requested two-/three-band symbolic obstruction does not
+occur. Set
+
+```text
+b1=b2=b3=b4=0,
+h=pi^3(pi-gamma), B=pi(pi-gamma), z=pi-gamma,
+Q=h^q+B,
+P=h^e+gamma+2z=h^e+2pi-gamma,
+c=-1,
+```
+
+and set every other chart coordinate to zero. This point obeys all three gauges
+and all coefficient-space declarations. Exact differentiation gives
+
+```text
+J(B,2pi-gamma)=-gamma,
+J(h,2pi-gamma)=pi^2(2pi-3gamma),
+J(B,h)=-2h,
+
+J(Q,P)=-gamma
+       +q*pi^2(2pi-3gamma)*h^(q-1)
+       -2e*h^e.
+```
+
+Thus the `h=0` target equation and every level `1,...,q-2=2t-1` hold. The
+only residual levels are `h=2t` and `h=3t+1`. For any fixed low cutoff `H`,
+the same point satisfies all levels `0,...,H` once `2t-1>=H`. It also satisfies
+`h=0` together with any fixed number of highest levels for sufficiently large
+`t`, because its defects remain at those two moving middle levels. Therefore
+neither the bottom two/three bands nor a fixed two/three-high-band subsystem can
+have a uniform unit certificate.
+
+**CONTROL / SCOPE.** This is a point of a proper subsystem, not a pair with
+`J=-gamma`, not a representative of the four-tuple, and not an attainment
+claim. Its purpose is solely to prove consistency of the proposed fixed-band
+test.
+
+### 5.2 First changing bands and certificate support
+
+**MEASURED.** Under canonical tail renaming, the `t=2` and `t=3` systems agree
+at `h=0,1`; their first difference is `h=2`, where the later chart has the new
+boundary coordinates `p_(3),B` and `r_(3),A`. More generally, the systems at
+`t` and `t+1` first differ at low level `H=t`. From the high side, offsets
+`L=0,...,t-1` from `4t+1` each have one equation and offset `L=t` first has
+two, so `t=2` versus `t=3` first differs at high offset `L=2` as well.
+
+**MEASURED LIMIT / OPEN[CERTIFICATE-SUPPORT].** The charged `t=2` artifact
+contains the ordered generators and reduced basis `[1]`, but no Singular
+protocol, lift matrix, or representation of `1` in the input generators. A
+reduced basis `[1]` alone does not identify which original band generators its
+reductions used. Hence the literal first generator used by the `t=2` or `t=3`
+unit representation is not claimed. What is proved here is the first system
+divergence (`h=2`/`L=2`), the first nonzero affine-`t` high generator
+(`h=4t+1`), and the first level missed by the exact low-band witness (`h=2t`).
+
+### 5.3 The `pi^-1` tail
+
+**OPEN[DESCENT-ANCHOR].** This order chart is polynomial and deliberately omits
+the separate reciprocal-Laurent tail equations. The charged report identifies
+the required tuple coefficient and gives a constant-pivot series-reversion
+recipe, but does not supply the map into this growing family. Importing tail
+cancellations printed for a different Appendix-II row would be analogy. Thus the
+banded identity supplies a uniform local recurrence, while neither it nor a
+proved `pi^-1`-tail bridge currently supplies a uniform unit certificate.
+
+## 6. Controls, proof scope, and FALLACY-v2 audit
+
+**MEASURED (controls).** Each accepted fixed-`t` run checks its declared main
+ring and the extracted saturation component. The positive empty control
+`<c>:<c>^infinity` reduces `1` to zero; the negative nonempty control
+`<c-1>:<c>^infinity` does not. Equivalent Rabinowitsch controls use
+`<c,Tc-1>` and `<c-1,Tc-1>` where emitted. The exact actual-pair control
+`(pi,pi-gamma^2/2)` has `J=gamma` and reciprocal anchor degrees `(2,2)`, but
+its pi-degrees are `(1,1)`, so the K16 four-tuple classifier fails.
+
+**PROVED-HERE (logical wrapper).** The order chart omits additional Laurent
+conditions and is therefore a necessary superset of the requested locus. A
+characteristic-zero unit ideal after saturating by `c` proves the fixed-`t`
+target empty a fortiori. A nonunit or modular-only result would instead be only a
+chart/counting result and would not construct a target pair.
+
+**FALLACY-v2 audit.** No cv flag is identified with a place or cover series; no
+exit set or exit price is asserted. The actual-pair control is not promoted to a
+four-tuple representative. Monic h-division handles raw zero remainders without
+discarding a vanished-leader branch. The ring, generator order, coefficient
+field, saturation component, and controls are declared. Fixed-`t` certificates
+are not promoted to theorem (T) uniformly. No new exit-price assertion is made,
+so no `charge_basis=...` line is due.
+
+## 7. Typed verdict and reproduction
+
+Pending final write-up.

