# Constant-pivot preprocessing audit

## Scope and status

This directory contains a proof-preserving preprocessing of the **gauged
Theorem-1.2 necessary order-chart superset** for the (K=16) ray at
(t=2,3,4).  It does not impose the omitted tuple-level Laurent bridge, and a
nontrivial residual basis therefore remains only a counting-bound result.  It
does not promote finitely many (t)-wise calculations to a uniform theorem.

`triangular_preprocess.py` prepares Singular inputs but never launches
Singular.  Its deterministic symbolic audit has completed.  The prepared
programs contain:

- the safe target gauges already applied by the source builder;
- the independent actual-pair convention control
  (F=\pi, G=\pi-\gamma^2/2, J(F,G)=\gamma), explicitly not a (K=16)
  four-tuple witness;
- empty and nonempty Rabinowitsch wrapper controls in the declared main ring;
- the main equation (T c-1=0), hence the (c\ne0) component.

No claim about a (t=3) or (t=4) basis is made here until the corresponding
prepared program terminates and its output is recorded.

## Exact algebraic justification

At one preprocessing step let

\[
 R_i=k[V_i],\qquad I_i=(a_i x_i+b_i,E_i),
 \qquad a_i\in k^*,\quad x_i\notin b_i,
\]

where (k=\mathbb Q), or a good finite field, and (E_i) denotes all other
current equations.  Put (S_i=k[V_i\setminus\{x_i\}]) and define

\[
 \theta_i:R_i\longrightarrow S_i,qquad
 x_i\longmapsto -b_i/a_i,qquad y\longmapsto y\ (y\ne x_i).
\]

The inclusion (S_i\hookrightarrow R_i), followed by passage to the
quotient, and (	heta_i) induce inverse maps

\[
 R_i/I_i\;\simeq\;S_i/(\theta_i(E_i)).
\]

Indeed, (a_i x_i+b_i) is killed by (	heta_i), and in the other direction
(x_i-(-b_i/a_i)=a_i^{-1}(a_i x_i+b_i)) vanishes in the quotient.  Thus each
step is an isomorphism, not merely a projection or a necessary-condition
replacement.  Composing the steps gives the ring map recorded in each
`t*_ring_map.tsv` file.  The program independently verifies, by exact Sympy
expansion, that the fully composed map sends every original generator either
to its recorded residual generator or to zero.

No chart-dependent expression is inverted: every listed pivot coefficient is
a nonzero rational field constant.  The map fixes (c), so it extends to
(c^{-1}R), equivalently to the Rabinowitsch presentation obtained by adding
(T c-1) and fixing (T).  Consequently the original and reduced
(c\ne0) systems have isomorphic coordinate rings.  In particular, one
extended ideal is the unit ideal if and only if the other is.

For a modular run, the same proof is valid after reduction only when every
pivot remains nonzero and every recorded denominator is invertible.  The
driver checks this condition before emitting a modular program.  Including
the denominator (2) in the actual-pair control, the excluded
characteristics are:

| (t) | excluded characteristics | prepared primes |
|---:|---|---|
| 2 | (2,3,5) | none |
| 3 | (2,3,7) | (32003,32009,32027) |
| 4 | (2,3) | (32003,65521,1000003) |

